ibutor": null, "rationale": "Cross-origin POST /api/guess preflighted on most guesses; cors({ maxAge: 86400 }) makes it once per session."}, {"id": "docs_learnings_google_fonts_link", "label": "Google Fonts @import moved to <link> + preconnect", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/LEARNINGS.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "An @import starts a full round trip late; a <link> with preconnect to both origins loads earlier."}, {"id": "docs_learnings_lrc_markup_leak", "label": "LRC markup leaked into guessable words (2026-09-14)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/LEARNINGS.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Id tags ([ar:...] leaks the artist), word timestamps, section headers, instrumental filler; lines dropped outright not blanked; brackets are markup, parentheses (backing vocals) are sung. MIN_LYRIC_WORDS=20 counted after cleanup."}, {"id": "docs_learnings_songid_leak", "label": "songId in /api/round leaks the title", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/LEARNINGS.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Catalog ids are slugified titles; fixing needs an opaque per-day round id touching the wire contract, roundStorage and e2e helpers \u2014 noted, not fixed."}, {"id": "docs_learnings_hastext_substring", "label": "Playwright hasText is a substring match (2026-09-13)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/LEARNINGS.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Words from the day's song are effectively random input; locators must match exactly (anchored RegExp)."}, {"id": "docs_learnings_e2e_reuse_server", "label": "E2E from a worktree tested the main checkout's servers (2026-09-13)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/LEARNINGS.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "reuseExistingServer let Playwright reuse another checkout's dev servers; fixed with dedicated ports (15173/18787/19229), no reuse, and configurable API_PROXY_TARGET."}, {"id": "docs_learnings_missing_dev_vars", "label": "Missing worker/.dev.vars bit twice (2026-09-13)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/LEARNINGS.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Second occurrence promoted to standing rules: gitignored config is never a manual step (ensure-dev-vars via predev:worker), and missing config names itself (STATE_SECRET middleware check)."}, {"id": "docs_learnings_wrangler_state_version", "label": "Wrangler .wrangler/ state is version-specific", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/LEARNINGS.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Switching Wrangler versions broke workerd (_cf_ALARM column mismatch); rm -rf .wrangler fixes it; pnpm resolves different versions than npm ci."}, {"id": "docs_learnings_kv_binding_commented", "label": "KV binding shipped commented out; dev uses --var SIMILARITY_SAMPLE", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/LEARNINGS.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "wrangler deploy validates namespace ids so a speculative binding breaks deploy; prefer wrangler dev --var in npm scripts over .dev.vars entries for dev-only switches."}, {"id": "docs_learnings_resolvesong_split", "label": "resolveSong.ts split out for Node tooling", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/LEARNINGS.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Scripts under plain Node lack workers-types (caches.default); splitting resolution from caching is a real seam and keeps scripts type-checked."}, {"id": "docs_learnings_tsx_for_scripts", "label": "Run scripts via tsx, not Node type stripping", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/LEARNINGS.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Node's native stripping needs explicit .ts import extensions, which the codebase doesn't use."}, {"id": "docs_learnings_float32_tobecloseto", "label": "Float32 round-trips need toBeCloseTo", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/LEARNINGS.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "0.6 in a Float32Array reads back as 0.6000000238...; element-wise toBeCloseTo in embeddings tests."}, {"id": "docs_learnings_cross_origin_pages_worker", "label": "Pages and Worker on different origins: VITE_API_BASE_URL required (2026-09-12)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/LEARNINGS.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Unset VITE_API_BASE_URL makes the build call relative /api on the Pages origin with no Worker; set in deploy job, pinned by deploy-workflow.test.ts."}, {"id": "docs_learnings_webserver_race", "label": "Playwright webServer raced Wrangler cold start (2026-09-11)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/LEARNINGS.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "One webServer entry per port; a combined command with one URL only proves the fastest process is up."}, {"id": "docs_learnings_silent_fetch_failures", "label": "Fetch failures silently swallowed in the UI (2026-09-11)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/LEARNINGS.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author"